	Constructor is used to set the user defined default value to variable.

	 Benefits:
	 The constructor set the user-defined default values to variables.
	 Does not need to invoke this method (Constructor is a method).
	 Constructor invokes automatically when creating an object (new AreaCicle())

	 Constraints:
	 Constructor name must be same as Class Name.
	 Constructor can not return any value.

	 Types:
	 Parameterized Constructor
	 No Parameterized Constructor/No-arg constructor
